  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard in Kibana, so I haven't checked how the panels look. I also haven't checked that the rule has run yet. Its status was still \"pending\" right after creation.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) holds web access logs. Key fields include:\n- `response` (HTTP status code, stored as text)\n- `bytes` (response size)\n- `clientip` (client address)\n- `geo.src`, `geo.dest` and `geo.coordinates` (geography)\n- `extension`, `url` and `request` (what was requested)\n- `machine.os`, `agent` and `referer` (client details)\n- `tags`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-bb08c6e2 Web logs overview\" (id `affbe9b7-94ed-4ffd-8860-bd38be3efc54`) has six panels and defaults to the last 7 days:\n- Total requests\n- Average bytes\n- Unique clients\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Top 10 source countries\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-bb08c6e2 5xx spike\" (id `d694e5fb-6c23-4e5d-8cb8-002fee10c926`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- **Schedule:** it runs every 1 minute.\n- **Condition:** it fires when a 5-minute window contains more than 10 documents where `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]`.\n- **Actions:** none are attached, so a firing is recorded in Kibana but nothing is sent.",
